---
description: "Code style — comments and readability"
alwaysApply: true
---

- Write self-explanatory code (clear names, small functions) so comments aren't needed to explain *what* it does.
- Only comment *why*, for non-obvious decisions — a tricky workaround, a business-rule constraint, a deliberate trade-off. Keep it to one line where possible.
- No comment restating what the next line obviously does.
